{"nodes": [{"id": "datasets_hungarian_established_003_chapter6_case_system_doc", "label": "Chapter 6: The Case System", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "established/003_chapter6_case_system.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "datasets_hungarian_established_003_chapter6_case_system_case_system_overview", "label": "The Hungarian Case System (23 cases)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "established/003_chapter6_case_system.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Hungarian expresses grammatical relations through an extensive suffixal case system rather than prepositions because case marking is handled by the same agglutinative suffixation as everything else in the language; cases sit outermost (after plural/possessive suffixes) because they operate on the whole inflected word, and vowel harmony governs which allomorph surfaces for the same reason it governs plural/possessive suffix choice."}, {"id": "datasets_hungarian_established_003_chapter6_case_system_inessive_case", "label": "Inessive Case (-ban/-ben)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "established/003_chapter6_case_system.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Inessive is treated as the paradigm representative for 'other locative cases' because nearly every non-superessive locative case suffixes identically to it - only the superessive requires a different, always-linking-vowel pattern - so explaining inessive's suffixation rules economically explains most of the locative group at once."}, {"id": "datasets_hungarian_established_003_chapter6_case_system_locative_cases_group", "label": "Locative Cases Group (interior/exterior/near x motion-toward/static/motion-away)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "established/003_chapter6_case_system.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Hungarian locative cases are organized along interior/exterior/near axes crossed with motion-toward/static/motion-away, giving a systematic grid because spatial relations are decomposed into these independent parameters rather than lexicalized case-by-case, letting one suffix pattern generalize across many concrete spatial meanings."}, {"id": "datasets_hungarian_established_003_chapter6_case_system_oblique_cases_group", "label": "Oblique Cases Group (dative, instrumental, translative, causal-final, essive-formal, terminative, distributive, essive)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "established/003_chapter6_case_system.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Oblique cases are grouped as 'everything else' because they don't fit the locative spatial grid or the two grammatical cases; several originated as extensions of spatial/directional meaning into abstract domains (e.g. translative 'into' extended to 'becoming'), which is why more than one shows v-initial assimilation inherited from a shared historical source."}, {"id": "datasets_hungarian_established_003_chapter6_case_system_verb_case_government", "label": "Verb/Case Government", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "established/003_chapter6_case_system.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A single Hungarian verb can take different case-marked complements for systematically different meanings (Hiszek Janosban 'I believe in Janos' vs Hiszek Janosnak 'I believe Janos') because case substitutes for what English does with distinct prepositions or verbs - the case itself carries part of the semantic distinction, which is why a dictionary must list a verb's governed case alongside its meaning."}, {"id": "datasets_hungarian_established_003_chapter6_case_system_v_assimilation_instrumental_translative", "label": "v-Assimilation of Instrumental (-val/-vel) and Translative (-va/-ve) Suffixes", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "established/003_chapter6_case_system.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The instrumental and translative suffixes' initial v regressively assimilates to the stem's final consonant (baratommal, lannyal, vizze, borra) because Hungarian resolves consonant-final-stem plus v-initial-suffix clusters by full place assimilation rather than by inserting a linking vowel, marking these two cases as a distinct 'v-assimilating' family."}, {"id": "datasets_hungarian_established_003_chapter6_case_system_gyerekeire_triple_stack_example", "label": "gyerekeire triple-stack morpheme example", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "established/003_chapter6_case_system.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "datasets_hungarian_established_003_chapter6_case_system_konyvekben_case_stacking_example", "label": "konyvekben / konyvemben case-after-plural/possessive example", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "established/003_chapter6_case_system.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "datasets_hungarian_established_003_chapter6_case_system_doc", "target": "datasets_hungarian_00_book_triage_catalog_rounds_essential_grammar", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "established/003_chapter6_case_system.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "datasets_hungarian_established_003_chapter6_case_system_doc", "target": "datasets_hungarian_established_003_chapter6_case_system_case_system_overview", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "established/003_chapter6_case_system.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "datasets_hungarian_established_003_chapter6_case_system_doc", "target": "datasets_hungarian_established_003_chapter6_case_system_inessive_case", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "established/003_chapter6_case_system.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "datasets_hungarian_established_003_chapter6_case_system_doc", "target": "datasets_hungarian_established_003_chapter6_case_system_locative_cases_group", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "established/003_chapter6_case_system.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "datasets_hungarian_established_003_chapter6_case_system_doc", "target": "datasets_hungarian_established_003_chapter6_case_system_oblique_cases_group", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "established/003_chapter6_case_system.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "datasets_hungarian_established_003_chapter6_case_system_doc", "target": "datasets_hungarian_established_003_chapter6_case_system_verb_case_government", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "established/003_chapter6_case_system.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "datasets_hungarian_established_003_chapter6_case_system_doc", "target": "datasets_hungarian_established_003_chapter6_case_system_v_assimilation_instrumental_translative", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "established/003_chapter6_case_system.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "datasets_hungarian_established_003_chapter6_case_system_doc", "target": "datasets_hungarian_established_003_chapter6_case_system_gyerekeire_triple_stack_example", "relation": 